281 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 239 0 R
/E (Brain tumours require highly accurate detection, segmentation, and continuous monitoring to support timely clinical decisions. Traditional manual analysis of MRI scans is slow, subjective, and limited by human fatigue. Existing AI systems mostly perform isolated tasks such as basic classification or 2D segmentation without understanding tumour evolution over time. This project aims to build an integrated, clinically oriented AI pipeline capable of 3D multimodal tumour segmentation, tumour classification, longitudinal tumour progression \(time-travel\) analysis, and federated multi-hospital learning. The system is motivated by the need for precision, explainability, scalability, and privacy-preserving collaboration in neurodiagnostics.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
